  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="98d3-57b5-96d1-a340" name="Carthaginian (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>CARTHAGINIAN ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.22-23), 600-146 BC.
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Battle Standard. Cavalry up to a quarter of the points; Infantry at least a quarter; Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to half; Special Units up to a quarter with one elephant per 1,000 points.
Phalanx: Punic citizens and African infantry fight in a phalanx (see the Ancient Greek rule), but may have unit standards and an Army Standard Bearer; the Oracles rule does not apply.
Allies from other lists (not built here: make a separate small roster): Numidians (Barbarian Light Cavalry, Warriors, Skirmishers), Celts (Barbarian Noble Cavalry or Warriors; not Fanatic Warriors) and Greeks (Hoplites including Spartans but not Sacred Band, and Skirmishers except Cretans, from the Ancient Greek list; no Oracles, no unit standards). All are subject to the Allies &amp; Mercenaries and Warband rules.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 50%
  Special Units: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
